    {
      "title": "Finishing Touches",
      "slug": "finishing-touches",
      "displayOrder": 100,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 254,
        "lessonOrder": 100
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Adjust the underarm seam to your liking. (There is only 1 armhole!)<br><i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> The original side seam split is 5\" (13cm)<br>\r\n<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Make the armhole opening as large as you like.\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-12-xs\"><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/36/underarm_seam.jpg\"></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-12-xs\"><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/36/underarm_seam1.jpg\"></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 4173,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Side Seam",
          "slug": "side-seam",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3164,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n<div class=\"col-12-xs\">\t<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/36/how_will_you_finish.gif\"></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-12-xs\"><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/36/finishing_group.png\"></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 4175,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "imageGallery",
              "slides": [
                {
                  "src": "/challenge/images/v2/36/enveloppe/finishing_collar.jpg",
                  "caption": "This yarn adds an interesting touch to the foldover collar.<br>\r\nI finished mine with a crochet picot edge:<br><br>\r\n<li>Worked 1 row of single crochet around the entire neck edge.</li>\r\n<li>Turned the work around and created the picot edge with the purl side of the knitting facing me</li>\r\n<li>Slip stitch into the first single crochet<</li>\r\n<li>*Chain 3</li>\r\n<li>Slip stitch into the same single crochet<</li>\r\n<li>Slip stitch into the next 2 single crochet*</li>\r\n<li>Repeat from * to * around the neck opening</li>\r\n</ul>"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/challenge/images/v2/36/enveloppe/finishing_edge.jpg",
                  "caption": "This unusual crochet edge is easier than it looks! (please let me know the name for this stitch)<br>\r\nThe striped yarn gave an accent to the edges.  You might also consider using contrasting color.<br><br>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Knit side of the work facing</li>\r\n<li>Single crochet 1 row along the entire edge.</li>\r\n<li>Single crochet in the first single crochet</li>\r\n<li>*Work a double crochet about 3/4\" into the knitting</li>\r\n<li>Single crochet in the next single crochet*</li>\r\n<li>Repeat from * to * around the edge</li>\r\n</ul>"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/challenge/images/v2/36/enveloppe/finishing_sleeve.jpg",
                  "caption": "Just for fun, I picked up in the round and hand knit 2\" of 2x2 ribbing around the armhole opening."
                }
              ],
              "legacy": {
                "enableAudio": "0",
                "playAudio": "1"
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 4176,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
